%% title: Balance Update Flow (Event-Driven)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant TxSvc as transaction-service
    participant Kafka as Kafka\nopenbank.transaction.events
    participant BalanceSvc as balance-service\n(Kafka consumer)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL\n(optimistic lock)
    participant Outbox as outbox table
    participant KafkaOut as Kafka\nopenbank.balance.events
    participant AccountSvc as account-service\n(denorm cache)
    participant NotifSvc as notification-service

    TxSvc->>Kafka: TransactionCommitted\n{accountId, currency, amount, direction}

    Kafka->>BalanceSvc: consume event (at-least-once)

    BalanceSvc->>DB: SELECT FROM balance_movement\nWHERE (account, currency, referenceId, op)\n(idempotency check V8)

    alt already applied
        BalanceSvc-->>Kafka: ACK (skip duplicate)
    else first delivery
        BalanceSvc->>DB: BEGIN
        BalanceSvc->>DB: SELECT balances FOR UPDATE\n(version check — optimistic lock)

        alt CREDIT
            BalanceSvc->>DB: UPDATE balances\nSET booked_amount += amount\navailable_amount += amount\npending_amount -= amount (if pending)
        else DEBIT
            BalanceSvc->>DB: UPDATE balances\nSET booked_amount -= amount\npending_amount -= amount
        end

        BalanceSvc->>DB: INSERT balance_movement\n(idempotency marker, same tx)
        BalanceSvc->>Outbox: INSERT BalanceUpdated event
        BalanceSvc->>DB: COMMIT

        BalanceSvc-->>Kafka: ACK

        Note over Outbox,KafkaOut: Transactional outbox relay
        Outbox->>KafkaOut: BalanceUpdated\n{accountId, currency, bookedAmount,\navailableAmount, updatedAt}

        KafkaOut-->>AccountSvc: update denorm balance cache
        KafkaOut-->>NotifSvc: check low-balance threshold\n→ push notification if triggered
    end
